214.m:
Nāga is said to dwell in belching, and kūrma in opening the eyes;
[Page 278]
kṛkara in eating, and devadatta in yawning.

216.m:
Agni said:
Having thus performed the twilight rite, one should recite and meditate upon the Gāyatrī;
since it protects the disciples who sing it, as well as one's wife and life-breaths,

217.m:
and the imperishability of my lineage, and imperishable resolve in righteousness!
Agni said:
Praised by Vasiṣṭha in ancient times on Śrīparvata, Śambhu was pleased;

224.m:
Puṣkara said:
The prince must be protected by the ruler of the earth;
and he should instruct him in the treatises on duty, wealth, and pleasure, and in archery.

